/-!
# Blowing up and flatness

Let `M` be a finite module over a commutative ring `R`.  Blowing up an ideal `I ⊆ R` and passing
to the *strict transform* — the base change of `M` to an affine blowup chart with its
`a`-power torsion removed — improves the local structure of `M`.  This file collects the three
results of *More on Algebra*, Section 15.26 that make this precise.

Two models of the affine blowup chart occur, and both are kept exactly as the source states
them.  For `0BBJ` the chart is the concrete quotient-of-fractions ring `Blowup I a` and the
strict transform is `strictTransform` of `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Blowup.StrictTransform`
(Stacks Tag 053H).  For `0CZM` and `0CZN` the chart is `affineBlowupAlgebra I a S`, the
`R`-subalgebra of an arbitrary localization `S` of `R` away from `a` generated by the fractions
`y/a` with `y ∈ I`, and the `a`-power torsion is spelled as the primary component
`Ideal.primaryComponent _ (Ideal.span {a})`.  The containment of the second spelling of
"`a`-power torsion" in the first, `primaryComponent_span_singleton_le_torsion'` below, is what
lets one copy of the base-change machinery serve both families.

## Main results

* `exists_fg_ideal_strictTransform_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank` (Tag 0BBJ): if `M_f` is finite
  locally free of rank `r`, there is a finitely generated ideal `I` with `V(I) = V(f)` whose
  every affine blowup chart makes the strict transform of `M` finite locally free of rank `r`.
* `fittingIdeal_strictTransform_affineBlowup_eq_top` (Tag 0CZM): for `I` the `k`th Fitting ideal
  of `M` and any `a ∈ I`, the `k`th Fitting ideal of the strict transform on the chart `R[I/a]`
  is the unit ideal.
* `isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_strictTransform_affineBlowup` (Tag 0CZN): if moreover `M` is free of
  rank `k` at every prime outside `V(I)`, that strict transform is finite locally free of
  rank `k`.

## Implementation notes

All three statements are fully universe polymorphic, with the ring and the module universes
independent: `Module.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank` takes its ring in one universe and its module in
another, so Tags 0BBJ and 0CZN quantify over a ring, a module and — for Tag 0CZN — a localization
of the ring in three unrelated universes, just as Tag 0CZM does.  The shared machinery below is
stated at the same generality, so no binder has to be collapsed anywhere in the file.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BBJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BBJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CZM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CZM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CZN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CZN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped TensorProduct


universe u v w

/-! ### Shared machinery

The material in this section is used by more than one of the three tags below. -/

-- Isomorphism-invariance of the Fitting ideals is `fittingIdeal_eq_of_linearEquiv` in
-- `RingTheory.Fitting.Basic`.

/-- The two spellings of "`f`-power torsion": the primary component for the principal ideal
generated by `f` is contained in — in fact equal to — the torsion for the monoid of powers
of `f`. -/
private lemma primaryComponent_span_singleton_le_torsion'
    {A N : Type*} [CommRing A] [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] (f : A) :
    Ideal.primaryComponent N (Ideal.span {f}) ≤
      Submodule.torsion' A N (Submonoid.powers f) := by
  intro x hx
  rw [Ideal.primaryComponent_mem] at hx
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hx
  rw [Submodule.mem_torsionBySet_iff] at hn
  exact ⟨⟨f ^ n, ⟨n, rfl⟩⟩,
    hn ⟨f ^ n, Ideal.pow_mem_pow (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self f) n⟩⟩

/-- A submodule of `a`-power torsion elements localizes to zero away from `a`. -/
lemma localized'_eq_bot_of_le_torsion'
    {R M S : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (a : R) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalization.Away a S]
    (T : Submodule R M) (hT : T ≤ Submodule.torsion' R M (Submonoid.powers a)) :
    T.localized' S (Submonoid.powers a) (TensorProduct.mk R S M 1) = ⊥ := by
  rw [eq_bot_iff]
  intro x hx
  rw [Submodule.mem_localized'] at hx
  obtain ⟨m, hm, s, rfl⟩ := hx
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hT hm
  show IsLocalizedModule.mk' (TensorProduct.mk R S M 1) m s = 0
  rw [IsLocalizedModule.mk'_eq_zero, IsLocalizedModule.eq_zero_iff (Submonoid.powers a)]
  exact ⟨t, ht⟩

/-- Base changing a strict transform back to a localization away from `a` recovers the plain
base change: killing `a`-power torsion is invisible after inverting `a`. -/
noncomputable def baseChangeQuotEquiv
    {R A S M : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [CommRing S]
    [Algebra R A] [Algebra A S] [Algebra R S] [IsScalarTower R A S]
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (a : A) [IsLocalization.Away a S]
    (T : Submodule A (A ⊗[R] M))
    (hT : T ≤ Submodule.torsion' A (A ⊗[R] M) (Submonoid.powers a)) :
    S ⊗[A] ((A ⊗[R] M) ⧸ T) ≃ₗ[S] S ⊗[R] M := by
  let N := A ⊗[R] M
  let Q := N ⧸ T
  let e : ((S ⊗[A] N) ⧸ (T.localized' S (Submonoid.powers a)
      (TensorProduct.mk A S N 1))) ≃ₗ[S] (S ⊗[A] Q) :=
    (IsLocalizedModule.linearEquiv (Submonoid.powers a)
      (T.toLocalizedQuotient' S (Submonoid.powers a) (TensorProduct.mk A S N 1))
      (TensorProduct.mk A S Q 1)).extendScalarsOfIsLocalization
        (Submonoid.powers a) S
  exact e.symm.trans ((Submodule.quotEquivOfEqBot _
      (localized'_eq_bot_of_le_torsion' a T hT)).trans
    (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange R A S S M))

/-- The `k`th Fitting ideal of a localization of a finite module is the extension of the `k`th
Fitting ideal. -/
private lemma fittingIdeal_localizedModule_eq_map
    {R : Type u} {M : Type v} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M]
    (U : Submonoid R) (k : ℕ) :
    fittingIdeal (R := Localization U) (M := LocalizedModule U M) (k : ℤ) =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap R (Localization U)) (fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ)) := by
  rw [fittingIdeal_eq_of_linearEquiv (LocalizedModule.equivTensorProduct U M) k,
    (fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, v, v, u} (R := R) (M := M)).2.2.1 _ k]

/-- If an ideal dies in a localization at `U`, each of its elements is killed by a member of `U`. -/
private lemma exists_mul_eq_zero_of_map_eq_bot
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (U : Submonoid R) (L : Type*) [CommRing L] [Algebra R L]
    [IsLocalization U L] {I : Ideal R} (h : Ideal.map (algebraMap R L) I = ⊥) {x : R}
    (hx : x ∈ I) : ∃ s : U, (s : R) * x = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff U L x).mp
    (by simpa [h] using Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (algebraMap R L) hx)
  exact ⟨s, by simpa only [mul_comm] using hs⟩

/-- The strict transform of a finite module is finite over the affine blowup chart. -/
private instance strictTransform_finite {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {I : Ideal R} {a : R}
    [Fact (a ∈ I)] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M] :
    Module.Finite (Blowup I a) (strictTransform I a M) := by
  unfold strictTransform
  infer_instance

/-! ### Fitting ideals of strict transforms (Tag 0CZM) -/

/-- On the chart `R[I/a]` the ideal `I` becomes principal, generated by the image of `a`. -/
private lemma map_affineBlowupAlgebra_eq_span_singleton {R S : Type*} [CommRing R]
    (I : Ideal R) (a : R) (ha : a ∈ I) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    [IsLocalization.Away a S] :
    Ideal.map (algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S)) I =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S) a} := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro y hy
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    let d : (Submonoid.powers a : Submonoid R) := ⟨a, Submonoid.mem_powers a⟩
    refine ⟨⟨IsLocalization.mk' S y d, Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩⟩, ?_⟩
    apply Subtype.ext
    show algebraMap R S y = algebraMap R S a * IsLocalization.mk' S y d
    simp [d, IsLocalization.mk'_spec' S y d]
  · rw [Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ rfl
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (algebraMap R (affineBlowupAlgebra I a S)) ha

/-- **Stacks Tag 0CZM.** Let `M` be a finite module over a commutative ring `R`, and let `I` be
its `k`th Fitting ideal.  On the affine blowup chart `R[I/a]` associated to any `a ∈ I`, the
`k`th Fitting ideal of the strict transform of `M` — the quotient of `R[I/a] ⊗[R] M` by its
`a`-power torsion — is the unit ideal. -/
@[stacks 0CZM]
theorem fittingIdeal_strictTransform_affineBlowup_eq_top
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M]
    (k : ℕ) (a : R) (ha : a ∈ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ))
    (S : Type w) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalization.Away a S] :
    let I := fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ)
    let R' := affineBlowupAlgebra I a S
    let M' := (R' ⊗[R] M) ⧸
      Ideal.primaryComponent (R' ⊗[R] M)
        (Ideal.span {algebraMap R R' a})
    fittingIdeal (R := R') (M := M') (k : ℤ) = ⊤ := by
  dsimp only
  let I := fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ)
  let R' := affineBlowupAlgebra I a S
  let N := R' ⊗[R] M
  let f : R' := algebraMap R R' a
  let T := Ideal.primaryComponent N (Ideal.span {f})
  let Q := N ⧸ T
  have hfitN : fittingIdeal (R := R') (M := N) (k : ℤ) = Ideal.span {f} := by
    rw [(fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, v, v, w}
      (R := R) (M := M)).2.2.1 R' k]
    exact map_affineBlowupAlgebra_eq_span_singleton I a ha
  by_contra htop
  obtain ⟨p, hpmax, hle⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal
    (fittingIdeal (R := R') (M := Q) (k : ℤ)) htop
  have : p.IsPrime := hpmax.isPrime
  have hnle := ((fittingIdeal_local_generation_tfae k p).out 3 1).mp
    (Stacks.Fitting.exists_fin_span_atPrime_quotient_primaryComponent k f hfitN p)
  exact hnle hle

/-! ### Local freeness of strict transforms (Tag 0CZN) -/

/-- A localization of `R` away from `a` is also a localization of the chart `R[I/a]` away from
the image of `a`. -/
private lemma affineBlowupAlgebra_isLocalizationAway
    {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) (a : R)
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalization.Away a S] :
    let R' := affineBlowupAlgebra I a S
    IsLocalization.Away (algebraMap R R' a) S := by
  let R' := affineBlowupAlgebra I a S
  dsimp only
  show IsLocalization (Submonoid.powers (algebraMap R R' a)) S
  rw [isLocalization_iff]
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro y
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := y.property
    rw [← hn]
    show IsUnit ((algebraMap R S a) ^ n)
    exact (IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit (S := S) a).pow n
  · intro z
    obtain ⟨⟨r, s⟩, hz⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (Submonoid.powers a) z
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := s.property
    refine ⟨⟨algebraMap R R' r, ⟨(algebraMap R R' a) ^ n, ⟨n, rfl⟩⟩⟩, ?_⟩
    rw [← hn] at hz
    show z * (algebraMap R S a) ^ n = algebraMap R S r
    simpa only [map_pow] using hz
  · intro x y hxy
    refine ⟨1, ?_⟩
    simpa using Subtype.ext hxy

/-- A module with a basis indexed by `Fin k` is finite locally free of rank `k`. -/
private lemma isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_equivFun
    {A N : Type*} [CommRing A] [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N]
    (k : ℕ) (e : (Fin k → A) ≃ₗ[A] N) :
    Module.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank A N k := by
  refine ⟨ULift Unit, fun _ ↦ 1, by simp, fun _ ↦ ?_⟩
  let b : Module.Basis (Fin k) A N := Module.Basis.ofEquivFun e.symm
  exact ⟨(b.baseChange (Localization.Away (1 : A))).map
    (LocalizedModule.equivTensorProduct (Submonoid.powers (1 : A)) N).symm⟩

/-- If `M` is free of rank `k` at every prime outside `V(Fit_k M)`, then the `(k-1)`st Fitting
ideal of `M` dies in any localization away from an element of `Fit_k M`. -/
private lemma fittingIdeal_away_eq_bot_of_free_off_fittingIdeal
    {R : Type u} {S : Type w} {M : Type v}
    [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M]
    (k : ℕ)
    (hfree : ∀ (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime],
      ¬ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ) ≤ p →
        Nonempty ((Fin k → Localization.AtPrime p) ≃ₗ[Localization.AtPrime p]
          LocalizedModule.AtPrime p M))
    (a : R) (ha : a ∈ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ))
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalization.Away a S] :
    fittingIdeal (R := S) (M := S ⊗[R] M) ((k : ℤ) - 1) = ⊥ := by
  cases k with
  | zero => simp [fittingIdeal]
  | succ n =>
    rw [show (((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) - 1) = (n : ℤ) by omega,
      (fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, v, v, w} (R := R) (M := M)).2.2.1 S n,
      Ideal.map_eq_bot_iff_le_ker]
    intro x hx
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff (Submonoid.powers a) S]
    by_contra hnone
    push Not at hnone
    let K := (Submodule.span R {x}).annihilator
    have hdisj : Disjoint (K : Set R) (Submonoid.powers a : Set R) := by
      rw [Set.disjoint_left]
      intro y hyK hyPow
      obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := hyPow
      exact hnone ⟨a ^ m, ⟨m, rfl⟩⟩
        (by simpa [smul_eq_mul] using
          (Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton x (a ^ m)).mp hyK)
    obtain ⟨p, hp, hKp, hpdisj⟩ := K.exists_le_prime_disjoint (Submonoid.powers a) hdisj
    have : p.IsPrime := hp
    have hap : a ∉ p := fun hap ↦
      Set.disjoint_left.mp hpdisj hap (Submonoid.mem_powers a)
    have hIp : ¬ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) ≤ p :=
      fun hle ↦ hap (hle ha)
    obtain ⟨e⟩ := hfree p hIp
    have hpair := ((finiteLocallyFreeOfRank_fittingIdeal_tfae (R :=
      Localization.AtPrime p) (M := LocalizedModule.AtPrime p M) (n + 1)).out 1 2).mp
      (isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_equivFun (n + 1) e)
    have hmap : Ideal.map (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime p))
        (fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (n : ℤ)) = ⊥ := by
      rw [← fittingIdeal_localizedModule_eq_map p.primeCompl n]
      simpa using hpair.1
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_mul_eq_zero_of_map_eq_bot p.primeCompl _ hmap hx
    exact s.property (hKp ((Submodule.mem_annihilator_span_singleton x (s : R)).mpr
      (by simpa [smul_eq_mul] using hs)))

/-- **Stacks Tag 0CZN.** Let `M` be a finite module over a commutative ring `R`, and let `I` be
its `k`th Fitting ideal.  Suppose that the localization of `M` at every prime outside `V(I)` is
free of rank `k`.  Then the strict transform of `M` on the affine blowup chart `R[I/a]`, for any
`a ∈ I`, is finite locally free of rank `k`. -/
@[stacks 0CZN]
theorem isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_strictTransform_affineBlowup
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M]
    (k : ℕ)
    (hfree : ∀ (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime],
      ¬ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ) ≤ p →
        Nonempty ((Fin k → Localization.AtPrime p) ≃ₗ[Localization.AtPrime p]
          LocalizedModule.AtPrime p M))
    (a : R) (ha : a ∈ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ))
    (S : Type w) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsLocalization.Away a S] :
    let I := fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ)
    let R' := affineBlowupAlgebra I a S
    let M' := (R' ⊗[R] M) ⧸
      Ideal.primaryComponent (R' ⊗[R] M)
        (Ideal.span {algebraMap R R' a})
    Module.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank R' M' k := by
  dsimp only
  let I := fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ)
  let R' := affineBlowupAlgebra I a S
  let N := R' ⊗[R] M
  let f : R' := algebraMap R R' a
  let Q := N ⧸ Ideal.primaryComponent N (Ideal.span {f})
  apply ((finiteLocallyFreeOfRank_fittingIdeal_tfae
    (R := R') (M := Q) k).out 2 1).mp
  refine ⟨?_, fittingIdeal_strictTransform_affineBlowup_eq_top k a ha S⟩
  cases k with
  | zero => simp [fittingIdeal]
  | succ n =>
    rw [show (((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) - 1) = (n : ℤ) by omega]
    have : IsLocalization.Away f S := affineBlowupAlgebra_isLocalizationAway I a
    apply (Ideal.map_eq_bot_iff_of_injective
      (show Function.Injective (algebraMap R' S) from Subtype.val_injective)).mp
    rw [← (fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{w, max w v, max w v, w}
      (R := R') (M := Q)).2.2.1 S n, fittingIdeal_eq_of_linearEquiv
      (baseChangeQuotEquiv (S := S) f _ (primaryComponent_span_singleton_le_torsion' f)) n]
    simpa only [Nat.cast_add, Nat.cast_one, add_sub_cancel_right] using
      (fittingIdeal_away_eq_bot_of_free_off_fittingIdeal
        (R := R) (S := S) (M := M) (n + 1) hfree a ha)

/-! ### Making a finite module locally free by blowing up (Tag 0BBJ) -/

/-- An element of a quotient by an `S`-torsion submodule that is killed by a member of `S` is
zero. -/
lemma smul_eq_zero_of_quotient_torsion'
    {R M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (S : Submonoid R) (s : S) (x : M ⧸ Submodule.torsion' R M S)
    (h : (s : R) • x = 0) : x = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ x
  rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] at h
  rw [Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := h
  exact ⟨t * s, by simpa only [Submonoid.smul_def, Submonoid.coe_mul, mul_smul] using ht⟩

/-- Multiplication by an element that is injective on `M` stays injective on any localization
of `M`. -/
lemma smul_eq_zero_of_localizedModule
    {R M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (S : Submonoid R) (b : R) (hb : ∀ x : M, b • x = 0 → x = 0)
    (x : LocalizedModule S M) (hx : b • x = 0) : x = 0 := by
  let l := LocalizedModule.mkLinearMap S M
  obtain ⟨⟨m, s⟩, rfl⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.mk'_surjective S l x
  simp only [Function.uncurry_apply_pair] at hx ⊢
  rw [← IsLocalizedModule.mk'_smul (S := S), IsLocalizedModule.mk'_eq_zero,
    IsLocalizedModule.eq_zero_iff S l] at hx
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hx
  rw [IsLocalizedModule.mk'_eq_zero, IsLocalizedModule.eq_zero_iff S l]
  refine ⟨t, hb (t • m) ?_⟩
  simpa only [Submonoid.smul_def, smul_comm b] using ht

/-- If the `k`th Fitting ideal of `M` is generated by `b` and `M` surjects onto `N`, on which
multiplication by `b` is injective, then the `k`th Fitting ideal of `N` is the unit ideal. -/
lemma fittingIdeal_eq_top_of_surjective_of_regular
    {R : Type u} {M : Type v} {N : Type w} [CommRing R]
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [Module.Finite R N]
    (q : M →ₗ[R] N) (hq : Function.Surjective q) (k : ℕ) (b : R)
    (hfit : fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ) = Ideal.span {b})
    (hb : ∀ x : N, b • x = 0 → x = 0) :
    fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := N) (k : ℤ) = ⊤ := by
  by_contra htop
  obtain ⟨p, hp, hle⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal _ htop
  have : p.IsPrime := hp.isPrime
  let A := Localization.AtPrime p
  let L := LocalizedModule.AtPrime p M
  let P := LocalizedModule.AtPrime p N
  let lM := LocalizedModule.mkLinearMap p.primeCompl M
  let lN := LocalizedModule.mkLinearMap p.primeCompl N
  let q' : L →ₗ[A] P :=
    (IsLocalizedModule.map p.primeCompl lM lN q).extendScalarsOfIsLocalization
      p.primeCompl A
  have hq' : Function.Surjective q' :=
    IsLocalizedModule.map_surjective p.primeCompl lM lN q hq
  have hfitL : fittingIdeal (R := A) (M := L) (k : ℤ) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R A b} := by
    rw [fittingIdeal_localizedModule_eq_map p.primeCompl k, hfit, Ideal.map_span,
      Set.image_singleton]
  let K := LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.lsmul A L (algebraMap R A b))
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ :=
    exists_fin_generating_family_quotient_ker_lsmul_of_fittingIdeal_eq_span_singleton
      k (algebraMap R A b) hfitL
  have hK : K ≤ LinearMap.ker q' := by
    intro x hx
    apply smul_eq_zero_of_localizedModule p.primeCompl b hb
    show b • q' x = 0
    rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul A, ← q'.map_smul]
    show q' ((LinearMap.lsmul A L (algebraMap R A b)) x) = 0
    rw [show (LinearMap.lsmul A L (algebraMap R A b)) x = 0 from hx, map_zero]
  let qK : L ⧸ K →ₗ[A] P := K.liftQ q' hK
  have hqK : Function.Surjective qK := by
    intro y
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hq' y
    exact ⟨Submodule.Quotient.mk x, rfl⟩
  have hgen : ∃ g : Fin k → P, Submodule.span A (Set.range g) = ⊤ :=
    ⟨qK ∘ g, Stacks.Fitting.span_range_comp_eq_top g hg qK hqK⟩
  have hnle : ¬ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := N) (k : ℤ) ≤ p :=
    ((fittingIdeal_local_generation_tfae (R := R) (M := N) k p).out 3 1).mp hgen
  exact hnle hle

/-- An element of the `k`th Fitting ideal of a finite module is already in the `k`th Fitting
ideal of a finitely presented module surjecting onto it. -/
private lemma exists_finite_presentation_fittingIdeal_mem
    {R : Type u} {M : Type v} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M] (k : ℕ) (x : R)
    (hx : x ∈ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ)) :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (K : Submodule R (Fin n → R)), K.FG ∧
      ∃ q : ((Fin n → R) ⧸ K) →ₗ[R] M,
        Function.Surjective q ∧
        x ∈ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := (Fin n → R) ⧸ K) (k : ℤ) := by
  classical
  let h := Module.Finite.exists_fin' R M
  let n := h.choose
  let q := h.choose_spec.choose
  have hq : Function.Surjective q := h.choose_spec.choose_spec
  let A : Matrix (Fin n) (LinearMap.ker q) R := fun i j => j.val i
  have hxA : x ∈ minorIdeal A (n - k) := by
    simpa only [fittingIdeal, Int.not_lt.mpr (Int.natCast_nonneg k),
      ite_false, Int.toNat_natCast] using hx
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hxt⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_finite_of_mem_span hxA
  have hdet (y : t) : ∃ (r : Fin (n - k) → Fin n)
      (c : Fin (n - k) → LinearMap.ker q),
      (y : R) = (A.submatrix r c).det := ht y.property
  choose rows cols hcols using hdet
  let J := t × Fin (n - k)
  let v : J → (Fin n → R) := fun j => (cols j.1 j.2).val
  let K := Submodule.span R (Set.range v)
  have hK : K.FG := Submodule.fg_span (Set.finite_range v)
  have hKq : K ≤ LinearMap.ker q :=
    Submodule.span_le.mpr (Set.range_subset_iff.mpr fun j ↦ (cols j.1 j.2).property)
  let qK : ((Fin n → R) ⧸ K) →ₗ[R] M := K.liftQ q hKq
  refine ⟨n, K, hK, qK, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro m
    obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hq m
    exact ⟨Submodule.Quotient.mk z, rfl⟩
  · let B : Matrix (Fin n) J R := fun i j => v j i
    have he : ((Fin n → R) ⧸ Submodule.span R
        (Set.range fun j : J => fun i : Fin n => B i j)) ≃ₗ[R]
        ((Fin n → R) ⧸ K) := LinearEquiv.refl R _
    rw [fittingIdeal_eq_minorIdeal_of_presentation B k he]
    apply (show Submodule.span R (t : Set R) ≤ minorIdeal B (n - k) from ?_) hxt
    apply Submodule.span_le.mpr
    intro y hy
    apply Ideal.subset_span
    exact ⟨rows ⟨y, hy⟩, fun j => (⟨y, hy⟩, j), hcols ⟨y, hy⟩⟩

/-- If `M_f` is finite locally free of rank `k`, some power of `f` lies in the `k`th Fitting ideal
of `M`. -/
private lemma exists_pow_mem_fittingIdeal_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
    {R : Type u} {M : Type v} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M] (f : R) (k : ℕ)
    (hf : Module.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank (Localization.Away f)
      (LocalizedModule.Away f M) k) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, f ^ n ∈ fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ) := by
  let S := Localization.Away f
  let L := LocalizedModule.Away f M
  have hpair : fittingIdeal (R := S) (M := L) ((k : ℤ) - 1) = ⊥ ∧
      fittingIdeal (R := S) (M := L) (k : ℤ) = ⊤ :=
    ((finiteLocallyFreeOfRank_fittingIdeal_tfae
      (R := S) (M := L) k).out 1 2).mp hf
  have htop := hpair.2
  rw [fittingIdeal_localizedModule_eq_map (Submonoid.powers f) k] at htop
  have hmem : algebraMap R S 1 ∈ Ideal.map (algebraMap R S)
      (fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := M) (k : ℤ)) := by rw [htop]; trivial
  obtain ⟨s, ⟨n, rfl⟩, hn⟩ :=
    (IsLocalization.algebraMap_mem_map_algebraMap_iff (Submonoid.powers f) S _ 1).mp hmem
  exact ⟨n, by simpa only [mul_one] using hn⟩

/-- Inverting the image of `a` in `Blowup I a` inverts `a` over `R`. -/
private lemma blowup_isLocalizationAway
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) (a : R) [ha : Fact (a ∈ I)] :
    IsLocalization.Away a (Localization.Away (algebraMap R (Blowup I a) a)) := by
  let A := Blowup I a
  let S := Localization.Away (algebraMap R A a)
  have ht (x : R) : algebraMap R S x = algebraMap A S (algebraMap R A x) :=
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R A S x
  refine IsLocalization.Away.mk a ?_ ?_ ?_
  · rw [ht]
    exact IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_isUnit (S := S) (algebraMap R A a)
  · intro z
    obtain ⟨m, w, hw⟩ := IsLocalization.Away.surj (S := S) (algebraMap R A a) z
    induction w using Quotient.inductionOn with | _ p =>
    obtain ⟨n, x, hx⟩ := p
    refine ⟨m + n, x, ?_⟩
    have hclear : algebraMap A S (Blowup.mk ⟨n, x, hx⟩) *
        algebraMap A S (algebraMap R A a) ^ n = algebraMap A S (algebraMap R A x) := by
      rw [← map_pow, ← map_mul, mul_comm]
      exact congrArg (algebraMap A S) (blowup_of_pow_mul_mk I a ha.out n x hx)
    rw [ht, ht, pow_add, ← mul_assoc, hw]
    exact hclear
  · intro x y hxy
    rw [ht, ht] at hxy
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := IsLocalization.Away.exists_of_eq (S := S)
      (algebraMap R A a) hxy
    rw [← map_pow, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, Blowup.algebraMap_apply,
      Blowup.algebraMap_apply, Blowup.mk_eq_mk] at hn
    obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hn
    refine ⟨j + n, ?_⟩
    simp only [Blowup.ofRepr, pow_zero, one_mul] at hj
    rw [pow_add]
    linear_combination hj

/-- On the chart `Blowup (⟨f⟩ * J) (f * b)` the ideal `J` becomes principal, generated by the
image of `b`. -/
lemma blowup_map_eq_span_of_mul
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (J : Ideal R) (f b : R) (hb : b ∈ J)
    [Fact (f * b ∈ Ideal.span {f} * J)] :
    Ideal.map (algebraMap R (Blowup (Ideal.span {f} * J) (f * b))) J =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R (Blowup (Ideal.span {f} * J) (f * b)) b} := by
  let I := Ideal.span {f} * J
  let A := Blowup I (f * b)
  let g := algebraMap R A
  have ha : f * b ∈ I := Ideal.mem_span_singleton_mul.mpr ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩
  have hreg := blowup_image_a_mem_nonZeroDivisors I (f * b) ha
  have hfreg : ∀ z : A, g f * z = 0 → z = 0 := by
    intro z hz
    apply (mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff_left.mp hreg) z
    show g (f * b) * z = 0
    rw [map_mul, mul_right_comm, hz, zero_mul]
  apply le_antisymm
  · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro y hy
    have hyI : f * y ∈ I := Ideal.mem_span_singleton_mul.mpr ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    have hgy : g (f * y) ∈ Ideal.span {g (f * b)} := by
      rw [← blowup_idealMap_eq_span I (f * b) ha]
      exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem g hyI
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mp hgy
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    refine ⟨z, ?_⟩
    apply sub_eq_zero.mp
    apply hfreg
    rw [mul_sub]
    show g f * g y - g f * (g b * z) = 0
    change algebraMap R A (f * y) = algebraMap R A (f * b) * z at hz
    rw [map_mul, map_mul, mul_assoc] at hz
    exact sub_eq_zero.mpr hz
  · rw [Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff, SetLike.mem_coe]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem g hb

/-- If `M_f` is finite locally free of rank `k` and `f ∣ a`, the `(k-1)`st Fitting ideal of the
strict transform of `M` on the chart `Blowup I a` vanishes. -/
private lemma fittingIdeal_strictTransform_pred_eq_bot
    {R : Type u} {M : Type v} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M] (f : R) (k : ℕ)
    (hf : Module.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank (Localization.Away f)
      (LocalizedModule.Away f M) k)
    (I : Ideal R) (a : R) [ha : Fact (a ∈ I)] (hfa : f ∣ a) :
    fittingIdeal (R := Blowup I a) (M := strictTransform I a M) ((k : ℤ) - 1) = ⊥ := by
  let A := Blowup I a
  let a' := algebraMap R A a
  let S := Localization.Away a'
  let Q := strictTransform I a M
  have : IsLocalization.Away a S := blowup_isLocalizationAway I a
  cases k with
  | zero => simp [fittingIdeal]
  | succ k =>
    rw [show (((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) - 1) = (k : ℤ) by omega]
    have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap A S) :=
      IsLocalization.injective S (Submonoid.powers_le.mpr
        (blowup_image_a_mem_nonZeroDivisors I a ha.out))
    apply (Ideal.map_eq_bot_iff_of_injective hinj).mp
    rw [← (fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, max u v, max u v, u}
      (R := A) (M := Q)).2.2.1 S k]
    let eqv : (S ⊗[A] Q) ≃ₗ[S] (S ⊗[R] M) :=
      baseChangeQuotEquiv (R := R) (A := A) (S := S) (M := M) a'
        (Submodule.torsion' A (A ⊗[R] M) (Submonoid.powers a')) le_rfl
    rw [fittingIdeal_eq_of_linearEquiv eqv k]
    rw [(fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, v, v, u}
      (R := R) (M := M)).2.2.1 S k, Ideal.map_eq_bot_iff_le_ker]
    have hpair : fittingIdeal (R := Localization.Away f) (M := LocalizedModule.Away f M)
        (((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) - 1) = ⊥ ∧
        fittingIdeal (R := Localization.Away f) (M := LocalizedModule.Away f M)
          ((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) = ⊤ :=
      ((finiteLocallyFreeOfRank_fittingIdeal_tfae
        (R := Localization.Away f) (M := LocalizedModule.Away f M) (k + 1)).out 1 2).mp hf
    have hlow := hpair.1
    rw [show (((k + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) - 1) = (k : ℤ) by omega,
      fittingIdeal_localizedModule_eq_map (Submonoid.powers f) k] at hlow
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨⟨_, n, rfl⟩, hs⟩ :=
      exists_mul_eq_zero_of_map_eq_bot (Submonoid.powers f) (Localization.Away f) hlow hx
    have hunit : IsUnit (algebraMap R S f) := IsLocalization.Away.isUnit_of_dvd a hfa
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker]
    apply (hunit.pow n).mul_right_eq_zero.mp
    rw [← map_pow, ← map_mul]
    rw [hs, map_zero]

/-- **Stacks Tag 0BBJ.** Let `M` be a finite module over a commutative ring `R`.  If the
localization of `M` away from `f` is finite locally free of rank `r`, then there is a finitely
generated ideal `I` with the same vanishing locus as `f` such that, on every affine blowup chart
`R[I/a]` with `a ∈ I`, the strict transform of `M` is finite locally free of rank `r`. -/
@[stacks 0BBJ]
theorem exists_fg_ideal_strictTransform_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
    {R : Type u} {M : Type v} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M]
    (f : R) (r : ℕ)
    (hf : Module.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank (Localization.Away f)
      (LocalizedModule.Away f M) r) :
    ∃ I : Ideal R, I.FG ∧
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus ({f} : Set R) = PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set R) ∧
      ∀ a : I,
        let _ : Fact ((a : R) ∈ I) := ⟨a.property⟩
        Module.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank (Blowup I a) (strictTransform I a M) r := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_pow_mem_fittingIdeal_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank f r hf
  obtain ⟨n, K, hK, q, hq, heK⟩ := exists_finite_presentation_fittingIdeal_mem r (f ^ e) he
  let N := (Fin n → R) ⧸ K
  let : Module.FinitePresentation R N :=
    Module.finitePresentation_of_free_of_surjective K.mkQ K.mkQ_surjective
      (by
        show (LinearMap.ker (Submodule.mkQ K)).FG
        rwa [Submodule.ker_mkQ])
  let J := fittingIdeal (R := R) (M := N) (r : ℤ)
  let I := Ideal.span {f} * J
  have hJ : J.FG := (fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, u, u, u}
    (R := R) (M := N)).2.2.2.1 inferInstance r
  have hI : I.FG := (Submodule.fg_span (Set.finite_singleton f)).mul hJ
  refine ⟨I, hI, ?_, ?_⟩
  · ext p
    show ({f} : Set R) ⊆ p.asIdeal ↔ (I : Set R) ⊆ p.asIdeal
    simp only [Set.singleton_subset_iff, SetLike.coe_subset_coe]
    exact ⟨fun hfp ↦ (Ideal.mul_le_left : I ≤ Ideal.span {f}).trans
        (Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hfp)),
      fun hIp ↦ p.isPrime.mem_of_pow_mem (e + 1)
        (hIp (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_mul.mpr ⟨f ^ e, heK, (pow_succ' f e).symm⟩))⟩
  · rintro ⟨a, ha⟩
    dsimp only
    obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton_mul.mp ha
    let : Fact (f * b ∈ I) := ⟨ha⟩
    let A := Blowup I (f * b)
    let Q := strictTransform I (f * b) M
    apply ((finiteLocallyFreeOfRank_fittingIdeal_tfae
      (R := A) (M := Q) r).out 2 1).mp
    refine ⟨fittingIdeal_strictTransform_pred_eq_bot f r hf I (f * b) (dvd_mul_right f b), ?_⟩
    let q' : (A ⊗[R] N) →ₗ[A] Q :=
      (strictTransform.mkQ I (f * b) M).comp (q.baseChange A)
    have hq' : Function.Surjective q' :=
      (Submodule.mkQ_surjective _).comp (LinearMap.baseChange_surjective A hq)
    have hfit : fittingIdeal (R := A) (M := A ⊗[R] N) (r : ℤ) =
        Ideal.span {algebraMap R A b} := by
      rw [(fittingIdeal_basic_properties.{u, u, u, u}
        (R := R) (M := N)).2.2.1 A r]
      exact blowup_map_eq_span_of_mul J f b hb
    apply fittingIdeal_eq_top_of_surjective_of_regular q' hq' r
      (algebraMap R A b) hfit
    intro x hx
    apply smul_eq_zero_of_quotient_torsion' (Submonoid.powers (algebraMap R A (f * b)))
      ⟨algebraMap R A (f * b), Submonoid.mem_powers _⟩ x
    show algebraMap R A (f * b) • x = 0
    rw [map_mul, mul_smul, hx, smul_zero]

universe t

/-! ### Tag 053I: weak flattening by blowing up — the statement

Stacks Tag 053I says that for a local domain `(R, 𝔪)` with fraction field `K`, a finite type
`R`-algebra `S`, a finite `S`-module `M`, and any valuation ring `A ⊆ K` dominating `R`, one can
choose an affine blowup chart on which the strict transforms of `S` and `M` become flat and
finitely presented.

The conclusion is recorded here as the predicate `Stacks053IConclusion`, and it is **not yet a
theorem**: no declaration in this repository carries the `053I` tag, and 053I is still a gap in
the chapter-15 tracker. The predicate is kept because it pins the target — it elaborates, so every
typeclass the statement needs is available — and because the two documented deviations from the
source are visible in it. Those deviations are:

* the source conclusion is unsatisfiable when `R` is a field, so the hypothesis `𝔪 ≠ 0` is
  required; `Stacks.AffineBlowup.no_admissiblePair_of_maximalIdeal_eq_bot` records the degenerate
    case;
* clause (4) is stated over the chart `R[I/a]` rather than over `R`. The source says "over `R`",
  but its proof concludes with Tag 02JO(3), whose conclusion is flatness over the *stage* ring,
  and the over-`R` reading is false — the errata entry gives a counterexample valid for every
  admissible chart.

Clauses (1)–(3) are phrased on the `Blowup I a` chart by `IsAdmissibleBlowupChart`, the same chart
that clause (4) uses, so the statement is about one model of `R[I/a]` throughout. That this agrees
with the vocabulary of Tag 052M — in which the directed-system machinery for the eventual proof is
written — is the content of `isAdmissiblePair_iff_isAdmissibleBlowupChart` below, which rests on
the chart bridge `Stacks.AffineBlowup.blowupEquivAffineBlowupAlgebra`. -/

/-- Clauses (1)–(3) of Stacks Tag 053I, phrased on the chart `Blowup I a`: the ideal `I` is
contained in the maximal ideal and finitely generated, the fibre ring of `R → R[I/a]` at `𝔪` is
nonzero, and `A` has center on `R[I/a]` in the sense of `IsCenteredOn` (Tag 00I9(3)). -/
def IsAdmissibleBlowupChart (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] {K : Type v} [Field K]
    [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] (A : ValuationSubring K) (I : Ideal R) (a : R)
    [Fact (a ∈ I)] : Prop :=
  I ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R ∧
    I.FG ∧
    Ideal.map (algebraMap R (Blowup I a)) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) ≠ ⊤ ∧
    IsCenteredOn A (Stacks.AffineBlowup.affineBlowupImage I a Fact.out)

/-- The chart-model comparison for clauses (1)–(3): being an admissible pair in the sense of
Tag 052M is the same as `IsAdmissibleBlowupChart`, which is phrased on the `Blowup` chart. Only
the fibre clause differs between the two, and `Stacks.AffineBlowup.fibreNonzero_iff` identifies it.
-/
theorem isAdmissiblePair_iff_isAdmissibleBlowupChart {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    {K : Type v} [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] (A : ValuationSubring K)
    (I : Ideal R) (a : R) [Fact (a ∈ I)] :
    Stacks.AffineBlowup.IsAdmissiblePair R A I a Fact.out ↔ IsAdmissibleBlowupChart R A I a := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4⟩
    exact ⟨h1, h2, Stacks.AffineBlowup.fibreNonzero_iff.mp h3, h4⟩
  · rintro ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4⟩
    exact ⟨h1, h2, Stacks.AffineBlowup.fibreNonzero_iff.mpr h3, h4⟩

/-- Clause (4) of Stacks Tag 053I, on the chart `Blowup I a`: the strict transform of `S` is flat
and of finite presentation over `R[I/a]`, and the strict transform of `M` is flat over `R[I/a]`
and finitely presented over the strict transform of `S`.

The base ring here is the chart `R[I/a]`, not `R`; see the section docstring. -/
def StrictTransformFlatFinitePresentation {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R) (a : R)
    [Fact (a ∈ I)] (S : Type w) [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (M : Type t) [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module S M] [Module R M] [IsScalarTower R S M] : Prop :=
  Module.Flat (Blowup I a) (strictTransformAlg I a S) ∧
    Algebra.FinitePresentation (Blowup I a) (strictTransformAlg I a S) ∧
    Module.Flat (Blowup I a) (strictTransform I a M) ∧
    Module.FinitePresentation (strictTransformAlg I a S) (strictTransform I a M)

/-- The conclusion of Stacks Tag 053I: there is an affine blowup chart `R[I/a]` satisfying clauses
(1)–(3) on which the strict transforms of `S` and `M` are flat and finitely presented.

This is a predicate, not a theorem; see the section docstring for why, and for the two signed-off
deviations from the source statement. -/
def Stacks053IConclusion (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsLocalRing R] {K : Type v}
    [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] (A : ValuationSubring K) (S : Type w)
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [Algebra.FiniteType R S] (M : Type t) [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module S M] [Module R M] [IsScalarTower R S M] [Module.Finite S M] : Prop :=
  ∃ (I : Ideal R) (a : R) (ha : a ∈ I),
    @IsAdmissibleBlowupChart R _ _ K _ _ _ A I a ⟨ha⟩ ∧
      @StrictTransformFlatFinitePresentation R _ I a ⟨ha⟩ S _ _ M _ _ _ _
